{
    "llm_config": {
        "class": "ollama",
        "model_name": "qwen2.5:7b",
        "base_url": "http://127.0.0.1:11434",
        "temperature": 0.0
    },

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "mbd_verification_lead",
            "function": {
                "description": "Front-man MBD agent that coordinates Simulink model design, inspection, and verification."
            },
            "instructions": """
You are an Automotive Model-Based Design (MBD) Lead.
When the user asks to build, edit, inspect, or simulate a Simulink model:
1. Call 'simulink_executor' ONCE with a plain text 'task' and 'skill_topic' (e.g., 'building-simulink-models').
2. Never summarize skill documentation back to the user unless asked—always make sure 'simulink_executor' actually executes the model creation or edit in MATLAB/Simulink.
""",
            "tools": ["simulink_executor"]
        },
        {
            "name": "simulink_executor",
            "function": {
                "description": "Executes Simulink Agentic Toolkit MCP tools and loads MathWorks MBD skills.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "task": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Plain text description of the Simulink or MATLAB task to perform."
                        },
                        "skill_topic": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Name of the Simulink skill to load, e.g. 'building-simulink-models'."
                        }
                    },
                    "required": ["task"]
                }
            },
           "instructions": """
You control a live MATLAB/Simulink session via 'load_simulink_skill' and 'run_simulink_mcp'.
Never create a model literally named 'model_name'—always use the exact model name requested by the user!

To create and populate a Simulink model (for example, 'ev_battery_monitor'):
Step 1: Create and open the empty model safely using 'run_simulink_mcp':
  tool_name: "evaluate_matlab_code"
  tool_arguments: {
    "code": "if ~bdIsLoaded('ev_battery_monitor'), new_system('ev_battery_monitor'); end; open_system('ev_battery_monitor');"
  }
Step 2: Populate and wire blocks using 'run_simulink_mcp':
  tool_name: "model_edit"
  tool_arguments: {
    "model": "ev_battery_monitor",
    "scope": "root",
    "layout_mode": "full",
    "operations": [
      {"op": "add_block", "type": "Constant", "name": "SocInput", "ref": "c1", "params": {"Value": "80"}},
      {"op": "add_block", "type": "Gain", "name": "ScaleFactor", "ref": "g1", "params": {"Gain": "0.01"}},
      {"op": "add_block", "type": "Outport", "name": "NormalizedSoc", "ref": "o1"},
      {"op": "connect", "target": "#c1.y1 -> #g1.u1"},
      {"op": "connect", "target": "#g1.y1 -> #o1.u1"}
    ]
  }
Step 3: After 'model_edit' returns status 'success', report the created block IDs back to the user and stop.
""",
            "tools": ["load_simulink_skill", "run_simulink_mcp"],
            "allow": {
                "to_upstream": {
                    "sly_data": ["last_simulink_telemetry"]
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "load_simulink_skill",
            "class": "simulink_bridge.LoadSimulinkSkill",
            "function": {
                "description": "Loads official MathWorks SKILL.md instructions and MCP tool schemas.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "skill_topic": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "Skill name to load, e.g. 'building-simulink-models'."
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        {
            "name": "run_simulink_mcp",
            "class": "simulink_bridge.SimulinkMcpBridge",
            "function": {
                "description": "Calls a tool on the MATLAB/Simulink MCP Server.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "tool_name": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "description": "MCP tool name: 'evaluate_matlab_code', 'model_edit', 'model_overview', 'model_read', 'model_check', 'model_read_diagnostics', or 'list_available_tools'."
                        },
                        "tool_arguments": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "description": "Arguments dictionary for the MCP tool."
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    ]
}